:25 PM, employee Tarek Bitar was traveling eastbound on FM 1585 approaching Upland Avenue. A third-party driver was traveling northbound on Upland Avenue.\n\nAccording to the employee, the third-party vehicle initially stopped at the stop sign but then proceeded into the intersection, entering the path of travel of Permian Unit 138. The employee stated he applied the brakes fully but was unable to avoid a collision. Impact occurred at an estimated speed of 65 MPH.\n\nFollowing the collision:\n\nThe third-party vehicle came to rest in the northeast corner of the intersection in the bar ditch.\nUnit 138 continued approximately 25 yards, crossed the oncoming lane, and came to rest on the north side of the roadway in the bar ditch.\n\nInjuries and Medical Response\n\nThe employee reported no injuries and did not require medical attention.\nThe third-party driver was alert and communicating with first responders at the scene but was transported by ambulance to the emergency room for evaluation.\n\nVehicle Disposition\n\nUnit 138 was transported to the Permian yard in Lubbock.\nThe third-party vehicle was towed by Lubbock Wrecker to their storage facility located at 3209 Slaton Hwy, Lubbock, TX 79404.\n\nCitations\n\nThe driver of the Jeep was ticketed at the scene of the incident.  ","location":"FM 1585 & Upland Ave, Lubbock TX","service_line":"Rentals","company":"Permian Equipment Rentals LLC","report_number":"80735650"},{"date":"2026-05-05","employee":"","type":"First Aid Only","description":"First Aid Only - Poly pipe employee had gotten to the yard and was stepping out of the truck and twisted his left knee. Employee was taken to Trinity Health clinic in Odessa and was Released Back to Work, No Restrictions.","location":"FM 1788 Poly yard","service_line":"Poly Pipe","company":"Butch's Rat Hole & Anchor Service Inc","report_number":"80703262"}],"assessments":{"total":7,"details":[{"date":"2026-05-05","assessor":"Cesar Herrera Garcia","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG 